data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Read the first pair of each stream and push `(key, stream index, label)` onto a heap. Then, in a loop, pop\nthe smallest entry, yield its key and label, read the next pair from the same stream, and push it. The\nstream index in the tuple does two jobs: it breaks ties in favour of the lower stream, and it keeps labels\nout of every comparison, because two entries never have the same index."},"hints_note":null}

